.TH GRAFANA-UTIL-DASHBOARD-CLONE-FOLDER 1 "2026-04-03" "grafana-util 0.13.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grafana\-util\-dashboard\-clone\-folder \- Duplicate dashboards from one live Grafana folder into another live folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grafana-util dashboard clone-folder [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Duplicate dashboards from one live Grafana folder into another live folder.
.PP
Use this when you need staging, review, or promotion copies of every dashboard in a folder without changing the source dashboards.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-source\-folder\-uid
source Grafana folder UID.
.TP
.B \-\-source\-path
source Grafana folder path, such as Platform / Infra.
.TP
.B \-\-target\-folder\-uid
destination Grafana folder UID.
.TP
.B \-\-target\-folder\-title
title to use when creating the target folder.
.TP
.B \-\-create\-target\-folder
create missing destination folders.
.TP
.B \-\-recursive
include child folders and their dashboards.
.TP
.B \-\-uid\-prefix / \-\-uid\-suffix
deterministic cloned dashboard UID rule.
.TP
.B \-\-replace\-existing
update existing target dashboard UIDs instead of blocking.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
preview without changing Grafana.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
acknowledge live writes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Duplicate dashboards from one live Grafana folder into another live folder.
.EX
grafana-util dashboard clone-folder --url http://localhost:3000 --token "$GRAFANA_API_TOKEN" --source-folder-uid infra --target-folder-uid staging-infra --dry-run --table
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgrafana-util\fR(1)
